.TH RUSTFMT 1 "September 2026" "Rust" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rustfmt \- format Rust source code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rustfmt
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ file ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rustfmt
formats Rust source files according to the Rust style guide.
Named files are rewritten by default, including files belonging to their modules.
With no file arguments, it reads Rust source from standard input and writes
formatted source to standard output.
.PP
Use
.BR cargo-fmt (1)
to format a Cargo package with its declared Rust edition.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-check
Check files without rewriting them. Report formatting differences and return
a nonzero status when changes are needed.
.TP
.BI \-\-emit " files|stdout"
Choose whether to rewrite files or print the formatted source.
Do not combine this option with
.BR \-\-check .
.TP
.B \-\-backup
Keep a backup when modifying a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-edition " edition"
Select the Rust language edition used to parse the source.
Supported editions are 2015, 2018, 2021 and 2024. Direct invocation defaults to 2015
unless configuration selects another edition.
.TP
.BI \-\-style\-edition " edition"
Select the Rust style-guide edition independently of the language edition.
Supported style editions are 2015, 2018, 2021 and 2024.
.TP
.BI \-\-config\-path " path"
Select the configuration search path.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " key=value,..."
Override configuration values on the command line.
.TP
.BI \-\-print\-config " default|minimal|current path"
Write the default, used, or current configuration. The
.B minimal
form requires an output path and input files;
.B current
prints the configuration that would apply to the given path.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-files\-with\-diff
List files whose formatting changed, or would change in check mode.
.TP
.BI \-\-color " always|never|auto"
Control colored output.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress ordinary output.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print additional information.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line help. Use
.B \-\-help=config
to list configuration options supported by this version.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the formatter version.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Options are read from
.B rustfmt.toml
or
.B .rustfmt.toml
in the project or a parent directory.
Command-line configuration overrides the file.
Some configuration options require a nightly formatter; consult
.B \-\-help=config
for the installed version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates success. Nonzero indicates an error or, when checking files,
formatting differences.
.SH EXAMPLES
Format a file using the 2021 language edition:
.PP
.nf
rustfmt \-\-edition 2021 src/main.rs
.fi
.PP
Check formatting without changing files:
.PP
.nf
rustfmt \-\-check src/main.rs
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cargo-fmt (1),
.BR rustc (1)
.PP
https://rust-lang.github.io/rustfmt/
